From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 02:00:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 40/44] feat(canvas): pick the renderer in Settings, and a
 label that names it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The render switches (doop:gpu, doop:zoom-pictures) were localStorage keys
set by hand in the console. Now they are a pick per browser:

- Settings → Appearance → Canvas renderer: GPU layer Auto / On / Off /
  "On, software GL too" (force), zoom pictures Auto / On / Off, and the
  label's switch. Auto removes the key, so the render trial decides, as
  before. The levels are fixed per page load, so a pick made after a
  canvas opened shows "applies when the page reloads" and a Reload button;
  before any canvas opened, the first one reads it.
- The renderer label: a button at the start of the zoom pill (floating or
  in the reviewer dock), off by default, a view option (doop:view-options
  .renderer) switched from the zoom menu or Settings. It reads GPU, DOM or
  Live (culling off), "· pictures" when zoom pictures are on, and a tag:
  auto (the trial picked), set (this browser did) or reload (a pick waits).
  Its tooltip says each factor's level and why (trial, set, not available
  here, trial off); its menu is the same pick, plus Reload and Hide.
- A GPU layer that was asked for and did not start (no hardware WebGL2
  without force, or a lost context) shows struck through: the store in
  gpuPictures.ts gets `failed`, set by StagePictures. Before, only a load
  the trial put on recorded the failure.
- decidedRenderTrial() reads this load's decision without making one, so
  opening Settings starts no trial load.

Prior art: Chrome's "Use graphics acceleration when available" is a
per-device renderer switch that applies on relaunch; a stats badge
(three.js stats.js, Mapbox GL's debug overlays) shows what is drawing.
This does both, per browser, and keeps the trial as the default.

Tests: rendererSetting.test.ts (keys, Auto, matching a load, label state),
the label in zoomMenu.test.tsx, viewOptions.test.ts.
